docs/BASELINE_AUDIT.md:317:| C19 | Low | `make lint` hides MyPy failures (`|| true`). `make format` rewrites files; no check-only format target exists. | `Makefile` |
docs/BASELINE_AUDIT.md:321:| C23 | Medium | Builds are not reproducible. There is no lock file. `requirements.txt` has unpinned `chromadb>=0.5.0`, `qdrant-client>=1.9.0`, and pydantic ranges. `requirements.txt` and `pyproject.toml` list different dependency sets. The run before the baseline failed on dependency resolution (3.12) and tests (3.10). | `requirements.txt`, `pyproject.toml`, CI run 36145575750 |
docs/BASELINE_AUDIT.md:328:| C25 | Medium | The production image installs dev, test, and docs tools (pytest, mypy, ruff, pre-commit, bandit, mkdocs), because `requirements.txt` contains them. The image is single-stage, so `build-essential` and `git` stay in the runtime image. | `Dockerfile`, `requirements.txt` |
docs/BASELINE_AUDIT.md:332:| C29 | Low | `SQLAlchemy` and `alembic` are required dependencies but are not imported under `ragbot/`. | `requirements.txt`, `pyproject.toml`, source search |
